# `pnpm format` is `prettier --write .`, and without this file that means the
# WHOLE repository. Measured on 2026-09-05: 50 files, among them
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-29-manifest-platform-design.md — the document
# CLAUDE.md's non-negotiables say never to edit — and pnpm-lock.yaml.
#
# So Prettier owns the TypeScript workspace and nothing else. Everything below
# is either prose whose line breaks are deliberate, generated, or config that
# belongs to a running platform.
docs/
infra/
**/*.md
**/*.yaml
**/*.yml
pnpm-lock.yaml
node_modules/
dist/
drizzle/
.env
.env.example
blueprints/*/skeleton/
# A blueprint's starters are apps laid over that skeleton, copied into a project as they
# are (§25, P5a Task 10) — an app's tree, for the reason fixtures/ below is excluded.
blueprints/*/starters/
# An APP's own tree, standing in for something Manifest did not write. The same
# reason the blueprint skeleton is excluded, and the same principle D13 enforces at
# build time: the platform does not rewrite an application's files. It also keeps
# `pnpm format` off an npm-generated package-lock.json.
fixtures/
# Generated by `pnpm contract:write`; its drift test compares bytes, and JSON.stringify
# does not wrap arrays the way Prettier does (P5a Decision 9).
packages/contract/openapi.json
# Generated by `pnpm contract:generate` from openapi.json; its drift test compares it with
# what openapi-typescript generates (P5a Decision 9).
packages/contract/src/schema.d.ts
# GitHub's own schemas, extracted from its REST description and kept VERBATIM — dated
# evidence of what GitHub said (the D5 plan, Task 4). Rewriting its whitespace would make
# the next re-extraction's diff unreadable.
packages/github-fake/conformance/github-schemas.json
